hsa|n|One who cuts; as, a stone cutter; a die cutter; esp., one who cuts out garments. ; That which cuts; a machine or part of a machine, or a tool or instrument used for cutting, as that part of a mower which severs the stalk, or as a paper cutter. ; A fore tooth; an incisor. ; A boat used by ships of war. ; A fast sailing vessel with one mast, rigged in most essentials like a sloop. A cutter is narrower end deeper than a sloop of the same length, and depends for stability on a deep keel, often heavily weighted with lead. ; A small armed vessel, usually a steamer, in the revenue marine service; -- also called revenue cutter. ; A small, light one-horse sleigh. ; An officer in the exchequer who notes by cutting on the tallies the sums paid. ; A ruffian; a bravo; a destroyer. ; A kind of soft yellow brick, used for facework; -- so called from the facility with which it can be cut.	v:167l,60,2~167l,60,2	n:fw8,130,16;167l,95,22~167l,95,22;fw8,130,16	N:1vm5,49,1~1vm5,49,1
hsa|a|One who cuts; as, a stone cutter; a die cutter; esp., one who cuts out garments. ; That which cuts; a machine or part of a machine, or a tool or instrument used for cutting, as that part of a mower which severs the stalk, or as a paper cutter. ; A fore tooth; an incisor. ; A boat used by ships of war. ; A fast sailing vessel with one mast, rigged in most essentials like a sloop. A cutter is narrower end deeper than a sloop of the same length, and depends for stability on a deep keel, often heavily weighted with lead. ; A small armed vessel, usually a steamer, in the revenue marine service; -- also called revenue cutter. ; A small, light one-horse sleigh. ; An officer in the exchequer who notes by cutting on the tallies the sums paid. ; A ruffian; a bravo; a destroyer. ; A kind of soft yellow brick, used for facework; -- so called from the facility with which it can be cut.	j:1vm5,65,3~1vm5,65,3	e:167l,50,1~167l,50,1
