hsd|n|of Cut ; The act or process of making an incision, or of severing, felling, shaping, etc. ; Something cut, cut off, or cut out, as a twig or scion cut off from a stock for the purpose of grafting or of rooting as an independent plant; something cut out of a newspaper; an excavation cut through a hill or elsewhere to make a way for a railroad, canal, etc.; a cut.	a:1vmy,54,2~1vmy,54,2	n:167l,55,6;2avt,27,1~167l,55,6;2avt,27,1	N:njg,49,3;1899,25,2~njg,49,3;1899,25,2
